  "notes": {
    "mara": "Interpretive placement in the sandy country between the branches. Vane walks many desert miles from here to the cataract; this draft gives that journey about 25 km.",
    "cataract": "The artwork retains its local metre scale. The fork and distant Evil Wood between its branches are textual; the 38 m drop, channel widths, geology and all regional coordinates remain interpretations.",
    "orchard": "The former lake basin is described in Chapter XII. Its restored shoreline in this draft is an interpretation of Vane’s prediction, not a surveyed shoreline.",
    "evil-wood": "The wood lies between the branches, far away when seen from the cataract. Its outline and restored island boundary are invented.",
    "hand-site": "The burial point disappears after restoration; it is retained here as an event marker. The river’s source is farther upstream.",
    "restored-upper": "A provisional long upper-river country. Its route, forests and distant mountain are grounded in the restored journey; its length and exact outline are invented.",
    "mountain-city": "A distinct mountain city beyond greater forests and a far plain. Its position, scale and architecture are provisional; it is not Bulika.",
    "estate": "Earth is a separate setting, reached through the mirror, garden and book transitions. It has no ordinary coordinate in the strange country.",
    "pine-portal": "The first pine crossing is not securely identified with the later baby-finding forest.",
    "palace": "Interior locations below share this palace marker. Their complete floor plan is not supplied by the book.",
    "carriage": "Vane sees the carriage before walking ten paces from the hall, then approaches it. This nearby placement is invented; the passage does not measure the full separation.",
    "hot-stream": "A deep, hot stream only a few yards wide, along the forest/plain boundary. It remains separate from the great river and wet in both states.",
    "bulika": "A roughly 700 m city footprint is a design choice. The walls, gardens, elevated palace and its connection to the square are grounded; building count and street plan are provisional.",
    "guide-forest": "A provisional forest fringe beyond the sandy upper country. The broad forest joins the fruit valley and hot stream; these contours and bearings are editorial.",
    "ivy-hall": "A local placeholder in the connected great forest. MacDonald describes a hall made of growing vegetation; its detailed scene remains to be built.",
    "plain": "A substantial grassland between the hot stream and Bulika. This draft allows about 27 km for the crossing; the novel supplies journey stages rather than measured kilometres.",
    "nests": "A local village of nests in large forest trees, with little undergrowth, beyond the giants’ reach but within foraging distance of the fruit valley. This is an unfinished terrain draft."
  },
